  "pitch_conclusions": [
    "004cdb37 loads logical surface width00e38d9c, subtracts visible sprite width, doubles it and stores destination row skip00d3b53c.",
    "0040fb7c reads physical pitch00e38d94 to calculate the initial y address. Each row copies visible_width*2 bytes then adds00d3b53c at0040fba8/0040fbc9. Thus this original dispatcher/copy composition advances by logical_width*2 between rows even when physical pitch is padded.",
    "This is not a proof that padded pitch is forbidden. The differential suite retains both packed and padded fixtures, compares all buffer bytes, and accepts padding writes only when native and C agree. Prefix/suffix guards and source preservation remain mandatory."
